00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,500
NASA's SPHEREx maps the whole sky in 102 infrared colours.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,700
Cold worlds near the Sun move through those pictures.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:09,700
MIRA. A public web observatory on NASA's SPHEREx data.

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:13,100
Point anywhere. Watch 27 years of NASA pictures play.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,400
See what moved, and how fast.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,400
Read its light. This one shows methane.

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,500
Measured on NASA's raw exposures. Checked by AI models.

8
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,000
17,604 stars caught moving. 635 in neither Gaia nor SIMBAD.

9
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:29,000
MIRA. Point at the sky. See what moved. Measure it.

